.TH QUANUXCTL-SPREADER 1 "February 2026" "QuanuX 1.0.0" "QuanuX Commands"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-spreader \- Manage QuanuX-Spreader Engine Deployment and Strategy Injection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl spreader
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B quanuxctl spreader
tool suite is the administrative interface for managing the 59ns QuanuX-Spreader Engine. It handles the "Cython Forge" pipeline, converting analytical Spread Math (JSON IR) into strictly-typed C++ via Cython transpilation, compiling it into a hardware-optimized binary, and securely deploying it over the NATS/ZMQ mesh to a waiting remote Execution Node.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B package \fI<STRATEGY_JSON_PATH>\fR
Forges the Spread Formula into a High-Frequency Executive Binary.

This complex command performs the following sequence:
1. Parses the Spreader JSON IR Schema.
2. Transpiles the structure into a Cython `_wrapper.pyx` (for Crucible backtesting) and a highly optimized `strategy_injected.hpp` (for the C++ 59ns loop).
3. Evaluates structural guards, failing the build if `StrategyState` exceeds a 64-byte L1 Cache Line.
4. Invokes the `spreader` CMake preset to perform a hardware-aware compilation (`-march=native`, `-O3`, `-flto`).
5. Extracts a SHA-256 binary hash and generates a cryptographic deployment manifest (`.sig`).

.TP
.B deploy \fI<BINARY_NAME>\fR
Securely deploys a forged binary to a remote Execution Node.

Before transmitting the payload, the command authenticates the executable against the companion `.sig` Forge Signature generated during the `package` phase. If the binary hash doesn't perfectly match the cryptographically signed manifest, the deployment instantly hard-aborts with a `CRITICAL SHM ERROR`, preventing the deployment of potentially bloated or rogue logic to the Exchange Co-Location.
.SH EXAMPLES
Forging a new CLZ4 vs CLF5 strategy from the JSON repository:
.RS 4
.EX
quanuxctl spreader package server/spreader-strategies/CLZ4_CLF5_Spread.json
.EE
.RE

Deploying the successfully forged binary to the live Execution Node stub:
.RS 4
.EX
quanuxctl spreader deploy quanux-spreader-063e07ea
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quanuxctl (1),
